{c: Chords: the writer's own chart}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Oh Lord my God
[D]You are a [D/G]mighty King
[D]Oh Lord my God
[D]You are a [D/G]mighty King
You are [Bm]clothed with [G2]hon[G]or
You are [F#m]clothed with [A/F#]majes[G]ty
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
And You [D/F#]walk on the [G]wings of the [A]wind
And You [D/F#]walk on the [G]wings of the [A]wind
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Oh Lord my God
[D/G]You are a flame of fire
[D]Oh Lord my God
[D/G]You are a flame of fire
At Your [Bm]voice, the mountains [G2]trem[G]ble
You make [F#m]darkness [A/F#]and its [G]night [D/F#] [G/E]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
How [D/G]beautiful You [D]are
How [D/G]beautiful You [D]are
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
At Your [Bm]voice, the mountains [G2]trem[G]ble
You make [F#m]darkness [A/F#]and its [G]night [D/F#] [G/E]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus 2}
And You [D/F#]walk on the [G]wings of the [A]wind
And You [D/F#]walk on the [G]wings of the [A]wind
And You [D/F#]walk on the [G]wings of the [A]wind
And You [D/F#]walk on the [G]wings of the [A]wind
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
How [D/G]beautiful You [D]are
How [D/G]beautiful You [D]are
{end_of_bridge}
